# Pip-Boy OS

The Pip-Boy OS (or Pip-Boy Operating System) is the 'soul' of the SPC 3000. 
This is my first ever Python code, so I used a [half made base](https://github.com/kelmes1/pipboy-pi) that I found online;


![Prenentation NV Gif](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/main/Software/documentation/screenshots/Record.gif)
![Prenentation NV Gif](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/main/Software/documentation/screenshots/RecordFO4.gif)

## AI Disclaimer
I used Gemini to transcribe human logic to Python code, this is to maximise library use, code optimization and time efficiency (while still learning how those comands work). I also did some direct modifications to the code (to fix some errors)

## 🚀 Quick Start / Requirements / Installation

All the software requirements are listed in the [requirements file](https://github.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/blob/main/Software/requirements.txt)
You can Install Pip-Boy OS from [PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/pipboy-os/#description) / from the [dist folder](https://github.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/tree/main/Software/dist) in this repo or you can directly download the source code in the repo. 
To quickly install and run the code put these 2 lines of code in the terminal:

        pip install pipboy-os
        python -m pip_boy_os.modules.main
        

## Preparations for Running the sourcecode
If you install the source code before running the Pip-Boy OS for the first time locally you'll need to run the file **init** (init.bash if you are using windows; init.sh if you're using linux) these files create various vital files and folders in the Pip-Boy OS (it generates the '**cache**' folder and the '**settings_secret**' file). **In case init doesn't compile/run**: you have to manually add the cache folder with inside 2 folders named '**map**' and '**places**' and you have to add a Python file inside **modules** called '**settings_secret**' with these lines of code.

        REAL_LOCATION = 'YOUR_LOCATION'
        LONGITUDE = 00.0000
        LATITUDE = 00.000
        GEOAPIFY_KEY = 'YOUR_GEOAPIFY_KEY'
 
REMEMBER: if you want to see the IRL Map you need to insert in the code above your information (doesn't need to be true) and Create/Insert your Geoapify API Key (at https://www.geoapify.com/get-started-with-maps-api/ in the "Project and API Keys" section); DO NOT insert the URL (it doesn't work).
## How To Run Sourcecode
To start the sourcecodecode you need to run [main.py](https://github.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/blob/main/Software/pip_boy_os/modules/main.py), running other codes inside the software will not work. The code works perfectly on PC, give it a try!

![alt text](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/main/Software/documentation/screenshots/image-1.png)

## Customization
The Pip-Boy OS that you can find in the repo can also be personalized using the [configure.py](https://github.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/blob/main/Software/configure.py) file or by using the **settings tab in the running code** (the position of the tab changes: in FO4 UI it's located in the DATA Menu, in the FNV UI it's a subtab of the General Tab in STATS). To move in the configure.py UI you use as inputs:
- **Numpad 2**: to move down
- **Numpad 8**: to move up
- **ENTER**: To change/select an option

(Always make sure that the Numlock is **ON**)
![alt text](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Danger2007/Survival-PC-3000/main/Software/documentation/screenshots/image.png)

### PARTS NOT MINE:

-**3d Model of the casing:** I used [This 3D Pip-Boy case](https://ytec3d.com/pip-boy/) as a base and then heavily modified it to make space for the hardwware

-**Pip-Boy menu:** I used [This Pip-Boy menu on github](https://github.com/kelmes1/pipboy-pi/tree/main) made by Kelmes1 as a base to develop my code (the code has suffered extreme changes, only a few files remained unchanged)

-**Clock Icons:** they are taken from the [Iconify archive](https://icon-sets.iconify.design/ ) and all have MIT or Apache 2.0 licensing (No attribution required, commercial use is allowed)

-**Songs:** they are taken from the [Internet Archive](https://archive.org/search?query=78+rpm+records&tab=all ) and are all 78 rpm songs from 1930s/1940s that are in the public domain

-**SFXs:** inherited from the base open-source repository of Kelmes1 (I don't know the origin of those SFXs; can be removed/replaced if required)

-**Images/Icons/2d Animations:** most images/icons/animations of the Fallout 4 UI are inherited from Kelmes1's repo (there are a few exceptions, like the [fatman animation](https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/fatman-m45-65bf0e5a4c304ca091d8dfa6a3a4fa8d) that I downloaded from sketchfab or the food icon that I downloaded from iconify). Almost all images from the Fallout New Vegas UI are from [The Fallout Fandom Wiki](https://fallout.fandom.com/wiki/Fallout_Wiki) (the only exception are the pipboy parts from the CND tab, which I acquired by cropping various online images of the original tab)

